Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:43:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?hyundai:=20KDMLink-derived=20telemetry=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20intake=20temp,=20accels,=20battery=20voltage,=20N-C?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ustom=20settings=20block=20->=20CarStateSP?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Everything else the KDMLink additions (patch 0046) can usefully feed on this car, wired the same
way as the fuel level (0047): CarStateExt.update_telemetry publishes four new messages, explicitly
subscribed at their real bus rates in get_can_parsers, straight onto CarStateSP:

  * intakeTemp     - EMS_453 D2 (degC, x0.75 - 48); 100 Hz. Validated on the owner's routes
                     (47-53 C while driving).
  * lateralAccel /
    longAccel      - ESP_49D (g; 16-bit centered / 12-bit Elantra-N layout); 10 Hz; plausible
                     magnitudes on the same routes (+-0.2 g gentle driving).
  * batteryVoltage - BATT_568 D3 (V, x0.1); 20 Hz; reads 12.2-13.7 V.
  * nModeEngine / nModeSuspension / nModeEsc / nModeExhaust / nModeRevMatch / nModeELSD /
    nModeSteering - N_MODE_4A0 N-Custom settings; 20 Hz; per-setting 0/1/2 = normal/sport/sport+
    style steps, 3 = unset/default. All zero in NORMAL drive mode; live in SPORT (bytes 0x55/0x50
    on the owner's routes) and N (0xFF/0x51).

Plain last-value reads - the parser holds each signal across update windows, nothing to debounce;
N-mode values are cast to int for the UInt8 capnp fields. Zero-initialised = not seen yet. No
other signal touched; Python only, no safety/firmware impact. Not on the comma-visible bus:
0x4E7 (AFR) / 0x5CE (fuel rail) / 0x5CF stay dongle-only - nothing to wire there.

Verified: 9 new tests (DBC layouts, packed-frame wiring incl. the real SPORT pattern, the
subscription regression) + full hyundai suite 608 passed + 261 subtests.
